</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.7 </span>What does generated inner speech look like during simulation?</h3>

<div id="A7.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since CVAE-generated inner speech lies in the latent embedding space, it is hard to fully interpret and visualize it. We thus employ a heuristic technique to analyze the inner speech during simulation by retrieving the top-2 training descriptions in CLIP’s embedding space at each update step. We use the cosine similarity to find the nearest training description and provide the value in parentheses. Here, we provide examples for both conditional and unconditional simulations and find how the top captions change along with the similarity score.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS7.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.7.1 </span>Conditional</h4>

